    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "The change tightens the file permissions on the built-in Pi extension from 0644 to 0600. The file contains Tempo-authored code, not secrets, but the directory `/opt/tempo/pi/` is static image content owned by root, and the extension reads session-local `mcp.json` from `$TEMPO_PROFILE_DIR`, which is already mode 0700 with the same 0600 file modes. No spec requires the extension file itself to be world-readable; the spec only states that it is copied to `/opt/tempo/pi/tempo-profile.ts` and loaded by pi through jiti. The existing image test checks `R_OK`, which still passes for the `tempo` user when running in the container. The change is consistent with the repository's security posture and does not introduce regressions in real contracts, failure paths, idempotency, security, build/runtime environment, tests, or spec conformance.",
